摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"An dsh plugin for role-based LLM retry&fallback strategy. 基于角色的模型重试备用策略插件","id":"gh:1326942966","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-llm-fallbacks","slug":"omdsh-dev/dsh-llm-fallbacks","topics":["deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","fallbacks","subagents"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"An dsh plugin for role-based LLM retry&fallback strategy. 基于角色的模型重试备用策略插件"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-llm-fallbacks"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | Chinese"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Automatic provider/model fallback chains for dsh (DeepSeek Harness): the plugin registers N **named "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"virtual chains**, each selectable in the model picker as **`FallbacksChain / <chain id>`** — a sessi"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"on routed to one walks that chain, so an LLM request that keeps failing on a listed code (auth, quot"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"a, rate limiting 429, …) is retried on the next available provider/model and tasks are not interrupt"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"ed by model problems. A session on any **real** provider/model has **no plugin fallback**: `llm-retr"},{"id":"p4s6","text":"y` alone handles it. Create a chain in the Fallbacks settings card, then select its `FallbacksChain "},{"id":"p4s7","text":"/ <id>` row to get it."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Works in both dsh front ends: the **web** profile (Settings → Plugins → Fallbacks card) and the **ds"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"h-tui** terminal profile (`/fallbacks` session diagnostics, `/fallbacks config` readback, and the `/"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"settings` fallbacks section for editing)."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Three core capabilities"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### Automatic model failover"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"A session routed to `FallbacksChain / <chain id>` — the root agent by selection, or a subagent whose"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" role points at that chain (「指定降级链」) — walks it: a request that fails on a listed code **before emit"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ting any output** is retried on the next available provider/model inside the same request, and the s"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"tep stays alive. Sessions on a real provider/model get no plugin fallback at all. No manual model sw"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"itching, and nothing happens until you configure a chain (empty `chains` is the only first-run state"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"ching, and nothing happens until you configure a chain (empty `chains` is the only first-run state)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- **Who gets a chain**: only sessions whose model selection routes to `FallbacksChain / <chain id>`."},{"id":"p9s2","text":" That is the root agent when the row is selected, and a subagent the seam mounted there at dispatch "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"(local backend, no explicit route on the request). A real provider/model selection — root or subagen"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"t — is left entirely to llm-retry.\n- **Triggers**: `triggerCodes` (default `AUTH` / `QUOTA` / `RATE_"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"LIMIT`) — **any** dsh failure code is accepted, including `CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED`, which fails ove"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"r to a larger-context candidate. Retryable failures (5xx, `TRANSPORT`, `TIMEOUT`, …) stay with llm-r"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"etry first; each of its retries re-enters the walk, which starts past the head that just went on coo"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"ldown.\n- **Partial output is committed**: the first **output** chunk commits the attempt — a block s"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"tart counts, a `usage` metadata chunk does not — and after commit a later failure is **not** switche"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"d inside the request, because yielded output cannot be unsent. The failure surfaces to the loop; rec"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"overy is llm-retry re-entry (a fresh walk) or the terminal error.\n- **Recovery**: a failed / switche"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"d-away model is held out of selection for `cooldownMs`, and `revertPolicy: cooldown-expiry` returns "},{"id":"p9s13","text":"to the primary model on expiry. The opt-in `recovery: half-open` mode (YAML-only) makes that return "},{"id":"p9s14","text":"evidence-driven instead of timer-based.\n- **Safety valve**: `maxSwitchesPerStep` caps switches per r"},{"id":"p9s15","text":"equest walk (attempts ≤ cap + 1) — chain loops cannot amplify latency.\n- **Visibility**: every switc"},{"id":"p9s16","text":"h is recorded in an info-level log line (from/to/role/reason/candidates) — no silent model switching"},{"id":"p9s17","text":" is recorded in an info-level log line (from/to/role/reason/candidates) — no silent model switching."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Peak/valley time slots"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Time slots are configured **per chain** and rotate that chain's effective entries by wall-clock wind"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"ows: the first row whose window contains the current moment replaces the chain's default entries for"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" the next request — the chain's own entries stay the last resort when no row matches. Rotation is a "},{"id":"p12s4","text":"routing seed, not a failure decision: it consumes no cooldown and leaves the failure walk (fallback "},{"id":"p12s5","text":"a failure decision: it consumes no cooldown and leaves the failure walk (fallback switch) untouched."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The figure shows the shipped card's structure: a **tab per chain** (`＋` adds one, `⋯` renames the la"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"bel or deletes the chain), and inside the selected tab — under its Chain name (链名称) field — the per-"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"chain blocks **Time slots (分时槽设置) → Default fallback chain (默认降级链) → Default model (默认模型)**, saved b"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"y that chain's own Discard/Save pair. The Subagents (子代理) section renders one collapsed role card pe"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"r role with its own save pair. The card also has a collapsible Advanced options (高级选项) disclosure be"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"low the role list (not shown in this figure)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Four frozen UTC+8 presets (the windows are code constants). `fallbacks.tz` is the config-level zone "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"every row's window is evaluated in; the card shows it read-only inside a custom row (`Asia/Shanghai "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"(UTC+8)`) while preset rows exist:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| Preset | Window |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| `liang-peak` | Monday–Friday 09:00–12:00 and 14:00–18:00 |\n| `liang-valley` | every other UTC+8 ti"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"me (complement of Liang Peak) |\n| `glm-peak` | Monday–Friday 14:00–18:00 |\n| `glm-valley` | every ot"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"her time (complement of GLM Peak) |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"GLM Peak and GLM Valley are offered in the card picker only when `zai-coding-cn` is configured. Cust"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"om rows take `start` / `end` (`HH:mm`, may wrap midnight) and an optional `days` list."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"→ Time slots"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Feature highlights"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- **Automatic failover** on a virtual route — a `FallbacksChain / <id>` session (root or role-stampe"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"d subagent) walks its chain on a listed failure code and the step continues; real-model sessions hav"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"e no plugin fallback. → details\n- **Context-window-aware fallback** — `CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED` fail"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"s over to a larger-context candidate; the switch is request-scoped (no cooldown). → details\n- **Peak"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"/valley time slots** — four frozen UTC+8 presets or custom windows rotate a chain's own effective en"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"tries. → details\n- **Role-based subagents** — a dispatch-declared role brings persona, notice row an"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"d badge to the child, and its optional `chain` pointer puts the child on `FallbacksChain/<id>`. → de"},{"id":"p20s8","text":"tails\n- **FallbacksChain in the picker** — select `FallbacksChain / <chain id>` to make the configur"},{"id":"p20s9","text":"ed chain the session route; any real model is served by llm-retry alone, with no plugin fallback. → "},{"id":"p20s10","text":"details\n- **Five bundled preset roles** — `reviewer` / `scout` / `security-reviewer` / `sonic` / `ta"},{"id":"p20s11","text":"sk`, declared on apply. → details\n- **dsh-tui surfaces** — `/fallbacks`, `/fallbacks config`, and a "},{"id":"p20s12","text":"`/settings` section with web-card parity. → details"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
